                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "There's only one thing I consistently dislike about this game. In sections where you need to jump to other platforms its easy to miss them. In the truck scene I presume is near the end of the game, its hard to hit the boss. I lack the vocabulary to explain what's causing these issues. I could say its because its a 2D game though its really a mix of the two. Though since there isn't a huge penalty for dying that makes this game enjoyable however dying to the same thing is not. Some sort of visual assistance setting would be helpful. \n\nMusic is good, I recommend that you buy the soundtrack. The clones are adorable and I like the sound they make when rescued. My other recommendation is to please be curious of what you may be able to do. It wasn't obvious to me that the gold statues were something beneficial to shoot, until lately I was curious to try.\n\nTLTR: Game design makes parkour & shooting projectiles at boss, visually difficult\n\nNote: In the time of writing this, I didn't beat the truck boss, it mad me calm quit the game.",
